  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Africa-EU Energy Partnership (AEEP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The multi-donor Action &#xbf;Africa-EU Energy Partnership (AEEP)&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;&#xbf;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(192, 0, 0);&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;is jointly co-financed by the European Union (EU) and the German Federal Ministry for Economic Cooperation and Development (&lt;em&gt;Bundesministerium f&#xfc;r wirtschaftliche Zusammenarbeit und Entwicklung&lt;/em&gt; - BMZ),&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(227, 108, 10);&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;and implemented by GIZ as part of the BMZ project &#xbf;Global Energy Transformation Programme (GET.pro)&#xbf;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;GET.pro is a European multi-donor platform, delivering on international energy and climate goals in a Team Europe spirit. The programme was commissioned by the BMZ in 2018 and is co-funded by the EU, Norway, the Netherlands, Sweden, and Austria. Total funding of GET.pro is EUR 162.2 million, out of which BMZ&#xbf;s contribution is EUR 52.9 million. This Action is a continuation of activities implemented by the AEEP as part of GET.pro, including &#xbf;One Stop Shop for Green Energy Investments and an Africa-EU Energy Partnership&#xbf;, NDICI CHALLENGE/2023/443-397.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;GET.pro is set up as a modular platform consisting of instruments that scale up their activities based on donor needs. The platform serves for unlocking efficiency gains in administrative processes that would be much more time-consuming if done on an individual donor-contract basis. This collaborative arrangement and platform setup are expected to enhance the Action&apos;s effectiveness and sustainability. &lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;One of the scalable instrument included in the platform is the Secretariat of the Africa-EU Energy Partnership (AEEP), whose activities are supported by this Action. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The duration of this Action is scheduled from 01 July 2025 to 1 April 2027 (21 months) with a total budget of 2,750,000 EUR (EU contribution 1,750,000 EUR and BMZ contribution 1,000,000 EUR). The GET.pro BMZ commission is running until 30 September 2028.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
